{"title":"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_DO_NOT_DO_(Painful_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 DO NOT DO (Painful Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(induction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (induction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c779d0ba2c47e7587d30a6d8c860c8d24603fa32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aee8b764fac3094f39f81a391d5f238f9d90a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> be the smallest prime which does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> Define the integer function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872459c9d9d954338e76df9ad1e93e015ca1b025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> to be the product of all primes less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aee8b764fac3094f39f81a391d5f238f9d90a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7266d3a58146e19bce08614e60fae5d60ce9c9ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(k)&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b848caf67e495bd58e3ce4593f4b9072811ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(k)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d2d5c5ccfac7a77b1fb26ca77d203f86697f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(k)=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> be the sequence defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cc2ebaf7b90d027f60713856ec8e83e3581b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a850a4b5611ffea0bf4e01512827194cee4112c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}X(x_n)=x_np(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b600a4c3c595339bc3f0fcec6c2fe43f3c94d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8aece3a141946dbf2641df780b6583eb59695b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_t=2090.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is basically the same as IMO Shortlist 1995 Sequences Problem 3. As a matter of fact, having solved the IMO SL problem immediately allowed me to solve this problem. ~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, for any prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c32b12acdc08a000c3de4222670c4c5b014ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 \\nmid x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" />.  This provides motivation to translate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> into a binary sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />. \n</p><p>Let the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2eee4b1ec49d0dd4e6f869b796b13f5ae9a53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{a_1} \\cdot p_{a_2} \\cdot p_{a_3} \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245a5501248a6ea24f520f76d4140cedf08e1674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th prime number. Then, for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98adf0a1aaf3fffbf6268a097c296cbbbca082a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, place a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />th digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />. This will result in the conversion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc2d6862045279d53d49e5ff1ed6339307a3419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 2, x_{2} = 3, x_{3} = 2 * 3 = 6, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplication for the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> will translate to addition for the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a5d7cf38519411c33a1df5223501f6fc0a675f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}X(x_n) = x_np(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> translates into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a3094346173d35afefd093ec04f81d83b9e4aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{n+1} = y_n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cc2ebaf7b90d027f60713856ec8e83e3581b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a56739c3b7709dbd0ee9de9b39165d594c0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> in binary. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64eb4619a5ed6f8ad5e7d6add0f5018c02ad6caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{10010101_2} = 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 19 = 2090$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"248\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb91f2ffc4a3fe4d660e4d79510e7c219aab0a38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 10010101_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea3f3f8a046594ac35c41529b32969596bf7922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: Just to clarify the step when we do the conversion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a5d7cf38519411c33a1df5223501f6fc0a675f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}X(x_n) = x_np(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> we are able to do it because adding 1 is equivalent to having one more factor of 2, adding 2 is equivalent to having one more factor of 3 and so on, and since we know there will be at most one factor of any prime, we can stay in binary, with each prime getting its own slot. Using this, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd3788519673fe61578e9f0f9adda5fd1f3b23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> corresponds to truncating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> in our binary-prime form to the last digits which are only ones, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fdf3b1970c9a41cf50ba3092aec609dac94d921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> corresponds to adding in a 1 to the first spot in our binary-prime form which does not have a 1. Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd3788519673fe61578e9f0f9adda5fd1f3b23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> will remove all of the 1s in the front and add a 1 in the first 0, which is directly behind all of the 1s that dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd3788519673fe61578e9f0f9adda5fd1f3b23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> just removed. This is exactly how regular binary addition works, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d2220a6fad653061ef149bdc63965813104374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} = x_n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> in the binary representation.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_DO_NOT_DO_.28Painful_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_DO_NOT_DO_(Painful_Bash)\">Solution 2 DO NOT DO (Painful Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 DO NOT DO (Painful Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We go through the terms and look for a pattern. We find that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb3fc2febb1988b36512463c821633812603961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72c124ddfd47559713c928caf4fc1a0c0ad80f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_8 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8cf7a3120b7d7d866d4559e44ddcf1882fb079c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444ed37b31454149658d66c44edbadeb03b6d72b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_9 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8858903d7668a52687c6bc7bd9da0d7e12e5329c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f23c4b83ec683085d50a4350774a23aba5743ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{10} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c591e984a8019defb7db9197863bacae0ab20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a8474ca398e15e02312eee61d4e0c334926ddb63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{11} = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc2cfbe4515648078867dfa17bc83ebc1f5ba33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb46cf4c282dc433a0a7e1ac854060e450a5456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{12} = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34bcdee5912b1969b77a542318ced0a6d4518f8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe9f9dda79c3b1b16d86472dcc2c47528693b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{13} = 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e32b1abf9b0b88411ba0685e758a9d526e3ffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_6 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d597eb3784d24342c09ebe01cb7a3479483d938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{14} = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/102643c7bede2291f88e390cbdb7fc58b881b32b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_7 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b889744b3630749ae52301e0d6adeb3c9406ab65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{15} = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Commit to the bash. Eventually, you will receive that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d5b8eb4ac333d66344144901583970463c6315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{149} = 2090$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea3f3f8a046594ac35c41529b32969596bf7922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> is the answer. Trust me, this is worth the 10 (20*) index points.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df94ad31a9946cba4ec8e94c658b4181b25f249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{-RootThreeOverTwo}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"173\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>NOTE: this only works for this problem because the answer is a low number like 149, and the numbers are small. DO NOT try this in a real problem unless it is your last one, as this is very risky. ~eqb5000\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28induction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(induction)\">Solution 3 (induction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (induction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> denote the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th prime.\nLemma: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951ac8ea2b1f56b2ccf61093a52a8cefa1e359e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+2^{k-1}} = P_k \\cdot x_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd32763f8a19d8356888f867f14455f202101152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq n \\leq 2^{k-1} - 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1a0ba85e6e5ac111256ba1b4c5ee991f590a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{\\mathrm{Proof:}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We can prove this using induction. Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/7178bde8be6b9f70157a770c72fc495185fa64d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^{k-1}-1} = \\prod_{j=1}^{k-1} P_j.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"130\" height=\"53\" /> Then, using the given recursion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b53346bd0a4824aa5a8f20d0616920fc3f889b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{k+1} = \\frac{x_np(x_n)}{X(x_n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"124\" height=\"43\" />, we would “start fresh” for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b13909ca3a139170540214525bf0d70ebdd0ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^{k-1}} = P_k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" /> It is then easy to see that then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c653ebb6c89e9c0ce893806263bd3b290e15eea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_n}{P_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"22\" height=\"35\" /> just cycles through the previous <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/6776069fc826067388ab544758e806cb876a84a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"11\" /> terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33bea6ad4aff41f31d5d5185767e27e3abf00f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ x_n \\},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> since the recursion process is the same and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> being a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not affected until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652e2f96d39578c446766c47df943fe9b63a05de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2 \\cdot {2^{k-1}} = 2^k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" /> when given our assumption <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7e56ca220630f76de6fc611f5d06808c110f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^k - 1} = \\prod_{j=1}^{k} P_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"109\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776939957eb5972a7febd68b21f0788c99943f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^k$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is now the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cbed7dc076f558ffc6d36d06df9060ba7d46c04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_{k+1} = p(x_{2^{n-1}}),\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc705c77682d3c5e9f4b0a5440eaf49c536cc2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a = p(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b963459bc9c0171321e02b9e81ac69c11c593a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is the only way that the aforementioned cycle would be affected. Specifically, by cancellation according to our recursion, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1a895c690b9bf204c64e564b99038f43292c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^k} = P_{k+1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> and the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> just starts cycling through the previous <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f1359891099537fb78a9c531694fc68c06c61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"11\" /> terms again until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4caa42129a782372c5b9d37c30b7b5e7dfa6bc42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2^{k+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"11\" /> when a new prime shows up in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe928bed127c83953c0ecaf0113c4280a5ca88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"11\" /> when it starts cycling again, and so on. Using our base cases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b443dc857d21a0ab315e3c619329d0dfcd3a3171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"11\" /> our induction is complete. \nNow, it is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098d9fe16fa105fff7376a3f83676051c6a8b5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2090 = 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 19 = P_1 \\cdot P_3 \\cdot P_5 \\cdot P_8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"298\" height=\"16\" /> and by Lemma #1, the least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51eb82acf000b3549713e0a3a2ad81fa08d4dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 | x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8dcd852eef850e45a35a411ad78cf01948f62dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7.$\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> By repeatedly applying our obtained recursion from Lemma #1, it is easy to see that our answer is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f12278441e2a4990231757ce13a73f2ea1a917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7 + 2^4 + 2^2 + 2^0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0eac1531cc4cd39d779738b6395dd8b7d05ae94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10010101_2 = \\boxed{149}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-fidgetboss_4000\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SXZ01azDCGE?si=_lIcna68SgCcG3av\">https://youtu.be/SXZ01azDCGE?si=_lIcna68SgCcG3av</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II\" title=\"2014 AIME II\">2014 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233216\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 583/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1775/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18057/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.411      1 -total\n 58.23%    7.227      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.05%    4.847      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12579:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233216 and revision id 290685. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}